# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# E2E environment configuration template
#
# Copy once per environment you run against:
#   cp .env.example .env.demo      (ships working values — see below)
#   cp .env.example .env.staging
#
# TEST_ENV selects the file: TEST_ENV=staging → .env.staging
# All .env.* files except this one are gitignored — never commit secrets.
#
# In CI these values come from Actions secrets (process.env) instead of a file,
# so you only need real .env.* files for local runs.
#
# ⚠ Data safety: only the environments listed in E2E_WRITE_ENVS run
#   create/edit/delete flows. Everything else is forced to @smoke (read-only)
#   by playwright.config.ts. Write specs must name entities with e2eName() and
#   clean up in afterEach.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── App under test ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The values below point at the public Sauce Demo app, so a fresh clone runs
# green with no setup. Replace them with your own application.
BASE_URL=https://www.saucedemo.com

# Origin for API-based data setup. Defaults to BASE_URL when unset.
# API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# API_TOKEN=
# API_TOKEN_PATH=/api/auth/token

# Skip the TCP reachability probe (globalSetup + the per-test guard) when the
# runner cannot reach the app by design. Leave unset for normal runs.
# SKIP_URL_CHECK=1

# Probe a different host than BASE_URL (an app served from another origin).
# E2E_GUARD_URL=

# ─── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use a dedicated test account. On write environments it must be able to
# create/edit/delete the data the specs exercise.
E2E_USERNAME=standard_user
E2E_PASSWORD=secret_sauce

# Apps with no login, or suites that log in per-spec:
# E2E_SKIP_AUTH=1

# ─── Parallel workers (optional extra accounts) ───────────────────────────────
# Workers default to 1 — the same user in two browsers session-kicks itself in
# most apps. Add complete extra pairs to run that many workers. Slots must be
# contiguous (_2, then _3, … up to _8). Headed mode always stays at 1 worker.
# Cap without removing accounts: E2E_WORKERS=2
# E2E_USERNAME_2=
# E2E_PASSWORD_2=

# Reuse an existing .auth/user.json instead of logging in again (useful when an
# identity provider is throttling you).
# E2E_REUSE_AUTH=1

# ─── Test data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tenant / organisation / workspace the specs operate in, when the app has one.
# Read via tenantName() — never hardcode it in a spec.
# E2E_TENANT_NAME=

# ─── Data-safety policy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated environments allowed to run write flows. Everything else is
# @smoke only. Keep production out of this list.
# E2E_WRITE_ENVS=demo,local,dev,qa,staging

# Deliberate local-only override for a normally read-only environment. Ignored
# when CI=true, so it can never be turned on by a pipeline variable.
# E2E_ALLOW_WRITES=true

# ─── Reporting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The build under test. A green report that does not name its release cannot be
# read back later as proof of anything — set this from your deploy pipeline.
# APP_VERSION=v2.4.0

# Turn ticket tags into Allure issue links, e.g. @PROJ-123.
# ALLURE_JIRA_BROWSE_URL=https://your-org.atlassian.net/browse
# ALLURE_ROLLUP_TAG=PROJ-100
# ALLURE=false          # skip Allure for one run

# ─── Evidence capture ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EVIDENCE=true TICKET=PROJ-123 → captures land in src/evidence/PROJ-123/
# HEADED=true                   → visible browser
#
# Publishing credentials (Jira / Confluence / Zephyr / Teams) live in a separate
# gitignored file, .env.publish — see publish.config.json and README → Publishing.
